    "transport": "Production transport/webrtc.FrameChannel, pinned Pion WebRTC/ICE, reliable ordered DataChannel. Experimental Go build overlays instrument SCTP and vary send admission, pacing and inbound delivery delay.",
    "socketModes": "Early batches use default Pion sockets. The mux batch explicitly uses one UniversalUDPMux and native UDP socket per PeerConnection, matching the production per-path socket structure. It still bypasses provider/session admission and product scheduling.",
    "emptyVideo": "recvonly video negotiated on every PeerConnection in every arm, including all baselines.",
    "parallelism": "Multiple independent PeerConnections/SCTP associations in one native process. Dynamic arms allocate 64 KiB frames (8-byte offset plus payload) from one shared work queue.",
    "crypto": "Production Go sealed records; production TypeScript revision/block verification and decryption, with four concurrent decoder operations and final ciphertext/plaintext SHA-256 checks.",
    "timing": "Browser start request after all channels open through last authenticated plaintext copy. Includes transfer slow start and record verification/decryption. Excludes file reading, sender sealing, ICE/DTLS setup, final whole-file SHA-256 calculation and disk output.",
    "memory": "Sender reads and seals the full fixture before timing. Receiver retains ciphertext and plaintext in memory. This is a transport-plus-decoder experiment, not the complete product transfer pipeline.",
    "repetitions": "Primary arms each have one declared warmup followed by three measured transfers. Arm order reverses on alternating repetitions; warmup values are retained. Screenings are exploratory, not equally repeated.",
    "latency": "Additional 80 ms FIFO delivery delay applied to inbound native SCTP above DTLS. Actual SCTP RTT is sampled every 100 ms. ICE, physical packet propagation, loss and congestion are not shaped.",
    "pacing": "Experimental per-association 32 KiB burst budget with timer sleeps and epoch reset; the requested MB/s is not a precision rate limiter or production control policy."
